text:
mika: Quick flag 90% layout issue on 320px: last table row overlaps with sticky footer when sidebar overlays. Screenshot: https://img.redwood.dev/ux/overlap-320-v2.png
andre: Can repro on iPhone SE. Action column wraps and increases row height, footer floats over it.
zoe: Likely caused by toggling body overflow + transform on sidebar. Mobile Safari recalculates viewport and sticky breaks.
mika: Thoughts on fix? reserve action column width or convert to compact action trigger?
andre: Both. Reserve 44px min for action affordance at <360px. Replace secondary cols with a single "Details" trigger that opens a stacked panel.
zoe: Accessibility: use labelled trigger ("Details"), aria-expanded, role="dialog" on panel, trap focus and return on close. Hit target >=44px.
qa-bot: Add test cases: iPhone SE Safari, Pixel 3a Chrome, VoiceOver, TalkBack, large-font and RTL.
mika: Also we should avoid position changes on body. Use fixed-position overlay for sidebar and avoid overflow:hidden on root.
andre: CSS prototype: ```css
@media (max-width:360px){
  .row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 44px;gap:8px}
  .action{min-width:44px;text-align:right}
  .table-wrapper{contain:layout}
}
```
zoe: Good. For discoverability prefer "Details" pill over icon-only. We'll run a small hallway test and A/B for icon-only behind flag `compact_action_icon` if needed.
design-bot: Draft PR created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/console/pull/3102. Feature flag: `compact_table_minimap`. Telemetry: `ui.table.compact_minimap.opened`.
mika: I'll canary behind the flag and add a perf marker around sidebar open to measure jumps. Tagging @qa once PR is ready. :thumbsup:
